4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) dry storage shelves (dust); 
B) ice machine - general surfaces on the backside (dust);
C) inside unused storage drawer (splash/buildup);
D) lower shelf where butter was stored (splash/buildup on all surfaces);  and
E) shelving on cook line above coolers and prep tables (dust/grease).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) walkin cooler shelves (debris accumulation);
B) prep cooler - inner surface of lid and inside the bottom (splash/debris);
C) dry storage shelving (buildup of spices/powders);
D) empty storage drawer on cook line (food crumbs/splash);
E) metal cart by back door (general buildup);
F) counter under microwave (food debris);  and
G) general surfaces of storage shelf on cook line where uncovered food was stored (dried splash).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general.
